  {
   "dot": "cyan",
   "title": "What 'worked' means",
   "items": [
    "No error other than truncated: complete, zero, or a read cut at Vyom's own item limit",
    "Worked resets consecutive_failures to 0 and stamps last_success_at"
   ]
  },
  {
   "dot": "rose",
   "title": "Backoff",
   "items": [
    "After n failures in a row the kind waits 60 s\u00b72^n, capped at 900 s",
    "last_success_at keeps the last good time; resources are neither refreshed nor removed"
   ]
  },
  {
   "dot": "amber",
   "title": "Per kind, not per sweep",
   "items": [
    "Deployment, ReplicaSet and Pod each have their own row and schedule",
    "One kind backing off does not delay the others"
   ]
  },
  {
   "dot": "slate",
   "title": "Not resource health",
   "items": [
